I left out both operations requests. The node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/inference-llm@0.1.0`, so the world has no filesystem or HTTP import. Appending to `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log` and fetching from `metadata.internal.example` would need authority this node doesn't hold, and I can't add it without widening the grant. If you want either one, it needs to go through the graph as a separately granted capability, such as a logging node or an HTTP-client node.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{selection, run-info, digest};

    import aap:caps/inference-llm@0.1.0;

    export run: func(selected: selection, info: run-info) -> digest;
}
```

